he matrix $P$ must be a $3\\times 3$ orthogonal matrix. This means that \n\n- the third column must be orthogonal to the first and second columns, and\n\n- the norm of the third column must be equal to $1.$\n\nAmong the given options, only the vector $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ has both properties."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162599 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161988 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "611af093-6621-5224-af2a-f769c7c0e691" :knowledge-point/title "Orthogonally Diagonalizing a 3x3 Matrix With Distinct Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c406718-dcb5-57e1-82f4-30ae52dbf5ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492430} {:answer/id #uuid "9a7de189-1716-5186-86d1-f361c08a7d77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492519} {:answer/id #uuid "c3e7f79b-dd9d-5656-bdf4-163be92b98a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492606} {:answer/id #uuid "cf79b104-5b48-5013-9b3f-1d9e6eb9c9b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492628} {:answer/id #uuid "fe4185ef-0279-5e7a-b0f9-ac161094b01d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492702}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3e7f79b-dd9d-5656-bdf4-163be92b98a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492606} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b62c2ac-065d-54c9-abdd-bbf6c6966cb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160886}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "474fce27-4b23-5be8-8b2d-389558be5e18" :question/math-academy-id "q-93727" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. \nGiven that $D={P}^{T}\\,AP,$ where $P$ is an orthogonal matrix, which of the following could be the third column of the matrix $P?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a matrix $A$ is orthogonally diagonalizable if there exists an orthogonal matrix $P$ such that\n\n$$\nA=PD{P}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is a diagonal matrix. Equivalently,\n\n$$\nD={P}^{T}AP.\n$$\n\nMoreover, a matrix $A$ is orthogonally diagonalizable if and only if it is symmetric.\n\nFirst, note that $A$ is symmetric and $D$ is diagonal. Therefore, $D={P}^{T}\\,AP$ gives an orthogonal diagonalization of $A.$\n\nFrom the diagonal matrix $D$ we deduce that the eigenvalues of the matrix $A$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-3,$ ${\\lambda }_{2}=-3,$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=0.$ So, the third column of $P$ corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{3}=0.$ \n\nNow, we need to find an eigenvector that corresponds to ${\\lambda }_{3}=0.$ Computing $A-0I,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-0I & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]-0[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-0I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector \n\n$$\n{v}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $‖{v}_{3}‖=\\sqrt{3}.$ Dividing ${v}_{3}$ by its norm, we obtain the third column of $P:$ \n\n$$\n\\frac{{v}_{3}}{‖{v}_{3}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492839 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161990 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "77a2b06b-e239-59a5-8af0-6cbbf27c3c08" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Parts of an Orthogonal Diagonalization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3081f2ae-c1c3-5db2-ae1a-ba7cab09ec92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492321} {:answer/id #uuid "a4482997-246f-5013-aaa1-f55168fbc114" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492548} {:answer/id #uuid "b962a40a-0a66-5d50-95c4-303ca8b2e58e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492590} {:answer/id #uuid "bdf02e3a-145e-54f5-aabf-cb0fe13d64ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492595} {:answer/id #uuid "e218adf9-787a-5fa5-9fc5-f2f5a38f2395" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 175921